      <h3 id="egress-traffic-control-networks-peer-external-destinations_ovn-k-egress-nodes-networks-peer" class="group scroll-mt-20">Using networks peer to control egress traffic towards external destinations<a href="#egress-traffic-control-networks-peer-external-destinations_ovn-k-egress-nodes-networks-peer" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p>Cluster administrators can use CIDR ranges in <code>networks</code> peer and apply a policy to control egress traffic leaving from pods and going to a destination configured at the IP address that is within the CIDR range specified with <code>networks</code> field.</p>
      <p>The following example uses <code>networks</code> peer and combines ANP and BANP policies to restrict egress traffic.</p>
